// Windows resource script -- compiled by windres (MinGW) into the .exe.
//
// The resource is named GLFW_ICON on purpose: GLFW's Windows backend
// registers its window class with whatever icon resource has exactly that
// name (see win32_window.c), so this one line gives you BOTH the icon shown
// for the .exe in Explorer and the icon in the window's title bar/taskbar,
// with no code changes. If it's missing, GLFW falls back to the default
// generic application icon.
GLFW_ICON ICON "icon.ico"
